  "chapter": 676,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 99 Chapter 676\n \n        MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 9832, entitled:\n \n    \"AN ACT to amend the labor law, in relation to enacting the New York\n        state fashion workers act\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This  bill  seeks to establish a registration system for model manage-\nment companies and sets forth the duties of model management  companies,\nas well as complaint procedures and penalties for violations.\n \n  I  fully  support the goals of this legislation to provide protections\nfor fashion workers, who have too often been subject to  unfair  working\nconditions  or  been  exploited  in  the workplace. However, changes are\nnecessary to clarify the duties of model management companies and brands\nto ensure they engage in contract transparency, as  well  as  provide  a\nsafe and non-exploitive working environment for models.\n \n  I  am  pleased  to  have  reached an agreement with the Legislature to\nenact these changes. On the basis of this agreement,  I  am  pleased  to\nsign this bill.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2024
 },
